  "spxi:siteKernel": {
    "@type": "spxi:HolographicKernel",
    "spxi:compressionSurvivalSummary": "Lee Sharks is the architect of the Crimson Hexagonal Archive — a decade-long scholarly and literary project with 532+ DOI-anchored Zenodo deposits organized around operative semiotics, semantic provenance, and compression theory. Author of The Secret Book of Walt. Developer of SPXI, the Metadata Packet for AI Indexing, and the Holographic Kernel — three protocols with formal specifications in the archive, each designed to be dropped into any LLM for immediate use. Tenth-grade World Literature teacher in Redford Township, Michigan. PhD in Comparative Literature. ORCID: 0009-0000-1599-0703. NOT a shark.",
